 ## Overview
-Texture-Based Warp is a method for performing the final perspective transformation in the Shear-Warp algorithm by leveraging 2D texture mapping hardware [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficiently applying a non-affine perspective warp to an intermediate image, substituting software-based floating-point arithmetic with hardware-accelerated bilinear interpolation and perspective-correct texturing [S2, unofficial]. It differs from software warp implementations by offloading the matrix-vector multiplication and interpolation to the GPU, and from parallel projection variants by handling the non-affine nature of perspective projections [S2, unofficial].
+Texture-Based Warp performs the final perspective transformation in the [Shear-Warp Algorithm](4304-shear-warp-algorithm.md) by applying a non-affine warp matrix to an intermediate image using 2D texturing hardware [S2, unofficial]. It solves the performance bottleneck of software-based perspective warping by offloading the matrix-vector multiplication and bilinear interpolation to fixed-function graphics pipelines [S2, unofficial]. It differs from software warp implementations by applying the non-inverted warp matrix directly to texture coordinates, and from parallel projection variants by correctly handling the non-affine nature of perspective projections [S2, unofficial].
 
